-**Data Structures:**
-- `grid`: A flat array of booleans. The voxel at 3D coordinates $(i, j, k)$ is accessed via the flattened index:
-  $$ \text{index} = i \cdot CUBE\_DIM^2 + j \cdot CUBE\_DIM + k $$
-  where $0 \le i, j, k < CUBE\_DIM$.
